<h3 class="text-center tmp-mb-4 text-normal">
  You now have access to GitHub Copilot.
</h3>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  This email outlines what’s included in your free plan with GitHub Copilot and how to start using it in your editor and on <%= link_to "github.com", "https://github.com" %>. Copilot Free includes access to frontier AI models from OpenAI and Anthropic with monthly usage limits.
</p>

<%= render Mail::ButtonComponent.new(text: "Get started with Copilot",
                                      url: copilot_immersive_url,
                                      classes: "btn-primary btn-large tmp-mb-3")
%>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  <b>What’s included:</b>
</p>

<ul>
  <li>
    <b>50 agent mode requests a month:</b>
    Use agent mode to debug issues, refactor code, and work through tasks in real time.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Model choice:</b>
    Access frontier models from Anthropic and OpenAI.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Custom instructions:</b>
    Guide Copilot's responses with your preferred style, conventions, or constraints.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>MCP integrations:</b>
    Integrate your tools and services using MCP servers. The GitHub MCP Server is available by default.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Work in your preferred IDE:</b>
    Available in VS Code, Visual Studio, Xcode, JetBrains, Neovim, Azure Data Studio, Eclipse, and Raycast.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>2,000 code completions a month:</b>
    Inline, context-aware code suggestions based on your repository and editor workspace.
  </li>
</ul>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  Not sure where to start?
</p>
<%= render Mail::ButtonComponent.new(text: "Try these Copilot Chat prompts",
                                      url: Copilot::EXAMPLE_PROMPTS,
                                      classes: "btn-primary btn-large tmp-mb-3")
%>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  <b>Copilot Settings</b>
  <br>
  <i>
    Telemetry in your free version of GitHub Copilot is currently enabled. By default, code suggestions that match
    public code, including code references in the VS Code and github.com experience, are allowed. You can adjust both
    telemetry and code suggestion settings in <%= link_to "Copilot Settings", copilot_settings_url %>.
  </i>
</p>
